--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -313,4 +313,7 @@ The campaign image is saved at most 1200 px on its longest edge (`CAMPAIGN_BANNE
 ### Google sign-in and the YouTube address
 During Google sign-in the browser may briefly show `accounts.youtube.com/accounts/SetSID`. That is Google's own step for keeping a Google login in sync across its sites; it happens on Google's side before Google sends the person back to `/auth/google/callback`, and nothing in this app asks for it or can turn it off. The app never uses YouTube data (scopes are `openid email profile`).
 
+### Email confirmation at sign-up (DL-165; migration `0049_email_confirm_required.sql`)
+When the site can send email (`mailer.enabled()`), a new password account is sent to `/confirm-email` right after signing up ("Check your inbox", resend, "Continue without confirming", "Wrong address?"). The confirmation email goes out at once (24-hour link). Until the link is opened the account can set up its profile and use everything except **creating a campaign** and **joining a campaign** (including by invite link); those redirect to the confirm page and come back afterwards. A banner on every page says what is missing. `users.email_confirm_required` is set at sign-up only, so accounts that already existed are never locked; with no mail server nobody is locked either. Google accounts start confirmed. The link also works when opened signed out or on another device (it proves the mailbox) and then shows the login page. To change what is locked, edit `_confirm_gate()` and its three call sites (`campaign_new`, `join_via_link`, `join_via_link_accept`). Tests: `tests/test_email_gate.py`.
+
 About and Contact pages (DL-25): `/about` (what the app does, in plain words) and `/contact` (shows `PRIVACY_CONTACT` as a mailto once set, otherwise says contact details are coming) are public and share the tab row with Privacy, Terms and Cookies. Replace the wording with real business details (DL-83) before launch. Test: `tests/test_privacy_page.py`.
